<title>LITHUANIA: INVESTMENT AGENCY HEAD RESIGNS - REPORT.</title>
<headline>INVESTMENT AGENCY HEAD RESIGNS - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian Investment Agency head Algis Avizhienis has resigned due to a lack of funding from the EU PHARE programme, newspaper Verslo Zinios said on Friday.</p>
<p>It quoted Avizhienis as saying that he decided to resign after PHARE stopped financing the agency in 1996 and after the government decided to merge it with the Export Promotion Agency.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted the head of the Vilnius EU delegation as saying he was satisfied with Avizhienis' work and that the PHARE funding had been delayed due to bureaucratic problems in Brussels.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
